  "body": "**What.** extend the A series past K = 45, or bound its remainder with a planted check of the geometric tail estimate behind `--tail`. Then rerun rational_fit.py with \u03bd \u2264 23 fitted. \n\n**Why.** at \u03bd = 19 the 1e-6 target is within a factor 2 of the data's remainder estimate, and Pad\u00e9's verdict changes with the tail. \n\n**Acceptance (can fail).** the \u03bd = 19 remainder estimate falls below 1e-7, and the K = 47 sums agree with the K = 45 tail-corrected sums within the estimate. A mutated tail (ratio doubled) fails that agreement. \n\n**Depends on.** the K = 45 scan setup (solver/inner_amp). That run took about 14 h on 3 processes.\n\n\nRecommended by #133's subagent (closing summary).\n",
